 ocean marine, and product recall insurance. Its personal lines offerings also include high value homeowners and personal insurance products. The company sells its insurance products in all 50 states, the District of Columbia, the Commonwealth of Puerto Rico, and the U.S. Virgin Islands primarily through a network of independent insurance brokers. Kinsale Capital Group, Inc. was founded in 2009 and is headquartered in Richmond, Virginia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael Patrick Kehoe J.D. | Chairman of the Board, CEO & President | Age 59 | Compensation: $4.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 711 people. Revenue per employee of $2.6M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 33%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $1.4M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $25K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Kinsale Capital Group, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $9.4B market cap on $1.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +32% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 28% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 21-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $990M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 53 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.07\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 61\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 1.1%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 5.5% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.7099727790150979},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $10.6M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-10614558.08},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Financial Services peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Growing faster than most Financial Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(KNSL) Movement as an Input in Quant Signal Sets","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/150/KNSL_Movement_as_an_Input_in_Quant_Signal_Sets_112226052002_1795342802.html","date":"2026-11-22","timestamp":1795342802.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Kinsale Capital Group (KNSL) Stock Still Looks Undervalued After A 99% Five Year Run","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance